![лестница](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b47783ab-e6f4-4d68-8764-39118cb5a741)



{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Step onto the bottom step of the stair climber.

### Step 2
If you are a beginner, hold the handrails lightly to help keep your balance.

### Step 3
Lean your upper body slightly forward from your hips.

### Step 4
Place your leading foot onto the step above, start the machine, and begin moving.

### Step 5
Keep your hands resting lightly on the rails and climb just like you would on regular stairs.

### Step 6
Shift your weight onto your front foot and step up, pushing through your heel and engaging your glutes and thighs.

### Step 7
Rise up onto that step completely.

### Step 8
Step up again with your other leg.

### Step 9
Keep holding the handrails lightly and take steady, deep breaths.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
⠀• Keep your back straight and your core engaged; avoid slouching.
⠀• Keep your knees in line with your feet—do not let them cave inward.
⠀• Place your whole foot flat on each step instead of stepping only on your toes.
⠀• Do not hang your full body weight on the handrails—use them only for balance.
⠀• Keep an eye on your heart rate and maintain steady breathing.
{{< /callout >}}
